WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.130
The John Wick franchise keeps raising the
bar at the box office and reaching new heights

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.000
with its stunts – but there's one thing
the series has never been able to overcome,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.000
until now.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.226
Warning: major spoilers ahead for "John Wick:
Chapter 4."

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:16.269
"You ready, John?"

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.781
"...Yeah."

00:00:19.781 --> 00:00:23.180
The first three "John Wick" movies successfully
hooked and maintained their audience with

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.400
a simple, repeatable recipe – John Wick
vs. a lot of doomed assassins.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.609
That winning formula was only limited by Keanu
Reeves' sheer will and director Chad Stahelski's

00:00:31.609 --> 00:00:33.117
violent imagination.

00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:36.590
There is a plot behind the violence, but it's
fair to say that it's not what the audience

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:37.739
is there for.

00:00:37.739 --> 00:00:41.370
As you watch the Boogeyman stab his way out
of a literal knife museum, normal narrative

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:45.520
concerns such as story progression and character
motivation take a back seat to the once-in-a-lifetime

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.753
spectacle of it all.

00:00:46.753 --> 00:00:51.570
In what other story would the hero deliberately
provoke a horse to kick their enemy — twice?

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.949
What other movie would spend nearly two minutes
showing you a man falling down every single

00:00:54.949 --> 00:00:59.320
step leading toward Sacre Coeur It's best
not to sweat the little things when you revisit

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.609
the Continental Hotel — instead, you should
just enjoy the ride, even if you're not quite

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:05.730
sure what's keeping it going in the first
place.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:09.830
Unfortunately, when one does stop to think
about the finer parts of this series' story,

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:13.981
it's hard to ignore one fact: for all the
ass-kicking action, John Wick is one of the

00:01:13.981 --> 00:01:16.152
most passive characters in modern cinema.

00:01:16.152 --> 00:01:20.750
In a genre defined by heroes taking the initiative,
he spends most of the three sequels in a completely

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.380
reactionary place.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:26.020
Instead of trying to accomplish a concrete
goal, he's mostly running around trying not

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.020
to die.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.960
For a series with less to offer, this would
be a damning issue.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.500
For "John Wick," it's a problem they don't
really need to solve.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.880
And yet, in "John Wick: Chapter 4," they solved
it anyway.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.680
The narrative thrust of the original "John
Wick" film is both simple and effective.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.200
John wants to kill the men that killed his
dog and stole his car, and his bloodlust will

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.139
not be satiated until he does so.

00:01:45.139 --> 00:01:49.340
This goal is largely accomplished by the end
of the first film and completely exhausted

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.509
by the opening moments of the second.

00:01:51.509 --> 00:01:55.670
In order to justify another "John Wick" adventure,
the series runs into a minor problem: how

00:01:55.670 --> 00:02:00.649
do you organically find motivation for a character
who essentially has nothing to live for?

00:02:00.649 --> 00:02:04.899
His wife is gone, his car is destroyed, and
his quest for vengeance is through.

00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:08.170
What else is there for John Wick to accomplish
but his own death?

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.360
"What?"

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.470
Though the three chapters that follow the
first film are each more thrilling than the

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:16.860
last, John's lack of motivation beyond an
indiscriminate thirst for violence and revenge

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.269
caused the quieter, emotional beats to feel
a bit weightless.

00:02:20.269 --> 00:02:24.020
In "John Wick: Chapter 4," however, characters
like Caine, Winston, and even the Marquis

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:27.080
finally force John to confront the emptiness
of his quest.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.480
The filmmakers use the climactic duel with
Caine at Sacre Coeur as a point of revelation

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:35.820
for John; both men want to escape from underneath
the High Table, but only one of them has a

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:36.820
life to return to.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:41.120
It's possible, then, to read John's sparing
of Caine as a recognition of this fact.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.980
By the time John begins to succumb to his
gunshot wounds, a welcome, yet unexpected

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:46.590
feeling of closure begins to set in.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:51.170
Yes, there are several spin-offs in development
and, yes, there's probably a chance John somehow

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.610
survived his "death" at the end of Chapter
4.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.380
But for now, his story is over.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:00.019
In the closing moments of Chapter 4, the series
has the courage to close the book on the franchise's

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:04.830
story in a way that acknowledges the grim
truth of John's circumstances in an operatic fashion.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:09.130
Finally, John gets to rest, secure in his
legacy as the most loving husband in the history

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:10.130
of planet Earth.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:13.959
And if it all ends up leading to him cheating
death for Chapter 5, at least we'll have the

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:17.799
feeling that it's a start of a new story,
and not just another episode of a seemingly

00:03:17.799 --> 00:03:18.799
endless quest.

00:03:19.102 --> 00:03:23.613
"Can a man like you know peace?

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:27.230
"Why not?"

